abstract: >-
  Wittgenstein Apartment (WA) is a sense-level behavioral predicate resource
  designed to bridge lexical-semantic representations of human action with
  character-relative action repertoires and downstream narrative, simulation,
  and planning systems. Release v1.0 contains 2,904 active Action Senses,
  541 Behavioral Predicate Families, 4,193 Goal Ontology relation rows, and
  eight Functional Projection views containing 1,392 projection rows.
keywords:
  - behavioral predicates
  - lexical semantics
  - computational semantics
  - knowledge representation
  - computational narrative
  - character modeling
  - action representation
  - digital humanities
